   138	B=D+11^T is invertible and
   139	B^{-1}=D^{-1}+(D^{-1}1)(1^T D^{-1})
   140	by the rank-one inverse identity in characteristic two. The generator evaluates
   141	that identity and carries both B and B^{-1} through independent row and column
   142	permutations. It never runs elimination on B.
   143	
   144	Easy regimes and attacks. Section 6.3 itself gives the IP_n factorization once
   145	the coordinates are aligned, which is why an exposed identity transform would
   146	be trivial. Dense rank-one camouflage and independent coordinate relabellings
   147	hide the local blocks. The tests include row/column outlier matchings, greedy
   148	nearest-unit columns, transposition, random invertible guesses, and the strong
   149	in-context near miss that correctly inverts every revealed block but omits the
   150	rank-one correction. Exact Gauss-Jordan is intentionally successful and is
   151	reported separately as the Track-B reference algorithm.
   152	""".strip()
