   292	def render(inst) -> str:
   293	    B = "\n".join(" ".join(map(str, row)) for row in inst["bilinear_matrix"])
   294	    n = inst["n"]
   295	    N = inst["communication_dimension"]
   296	    text = f"""Exact coordinate certificate for a PSD-rank upper bound
   297	
   298	All vector and matrix arithmetic in this problem is over GF(2): addition and
   299	multiplication are reduced modulo 2. Let x and y range over all binary column
   300	vectors of length n={n}. The displayed invertible binary matrix B defines the
   301	{N} by {N} nonnegative communication matrix W_B implicitly by
   302	
   303	    W_B(x,y) = x^T B y mod 2.
   304	
   305	Thus every entry of W_B is the ordinary integer 0 or 1. The standard inner-
   306	product communication matrix is IP_n(x,z)=x^T z mod 2. A binary n by n matrix
   307	Q is a change-of-coordinate certificate when
   308	
   309	    B Q = I_n over GF(2).
   310	
   311	This equation is equivalent to W_B(x,Qz)=IP_n(x,z) for every binary x,z, so Q
   312	is an exact column relabelling that transports any PSD factorization of IP_n to
   313	W_B. Matrix B, one row per line, is:
   314	
   315	{B}
   316	
   317	Return one change-of-coordinate certificate Q. It must be a JSON array of
   318	exactly {n} rows, each containing exactly {n} integers. Each entry must be 0 or
   319	1; booleans are not accepted. Row and column positions are 0-based, their order
   320	is the displayed order, and repeated rows are not allowed. Ordinary matrix
   321	multiplication is used before reducing each entry modulo 2.
   322	
   323	Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as one JSON object with the
   324	single key \"matrix\".
   325	Example format only: <answer>{{\"matrix\":[[1,0],[0,1]]}}</answer>
   326	Output nothing else inside the tags."""
   327	    mode = os.environ.get("GV_HINT_MODE")
   328	    if mode == "structural":
   329	        text += "\n\n" + STRUCTURAL_HINT
   330	    elif mode == "placebo":
   331	        text += "\n\n" + PLACEBO_HINT
   332	    return text
